d.line("`GuardrailDetector.__init__(client, guardrail_id, version, threshold, *, gate, usd_per_call=None, unmetered=False)`", "`GuardrailDetector.__init__(client, guardrail_id, version, threshold, *, gate, price: GuardrailPrice | None = None, unmetered=False)`, where `GuardrailPrice(usd_per_unit, unit_chars, max_chars)` is built from the three settings of 5.1 (same rule as the llm kinds: a gate, or `unmetered=True` said out loud, 5.3); `make(settings, deps)` (`guard/bedrock_guardrail.py:61`) reads `deps.gate`. In `check`, **after** the empty-text return (no request, nothing reserved) and the redaction, and **before** `apply_guardrail` (`guard/bedrock_guardrail.py:101`): (1) **length bound (security major F4: today the whole text is sent, `guard/bedrock_guardrail.py:98-106`, with no length bound):** a text longer than `price.max_chars` raises `SpendRefused(\"prompt_too_large\")` and no request is made; (2) `units = ceil(len(text) / price.unit_chars)`; `ctx = CallCtx(route=None, worst=price.usd_per_unit * units * GUARDRAIL_MAX_REQUESTS, kind=\"fixed\")`; `ticket = gate.admit(ctx)`; then `try:` the `apply_guardrail` request, `finally: gate.keep(ticket, ctx)`. The attempt is **kept** after success or failure (a guardrail answer carries no cost field, so there is no settle; `keep` adds it to the run's cost through `scope.kept`). `admit` runs the window check (S-1) and, from S-2a, reserves against the run's scope, or, on the approval summary screen, against `-unattributed` through `ScopedDetector` (5.5). **What is UNVERIFIED and what it can do (5.9 row 7):** whether the vendor bills this check per unit of text, per policy type or per request. The reserve is exact only if the operator's `usd_per_unit` and `unit_chars` describe the real bill; if not, the booked amount is wrong on every guardrail call and **is never corrected** (no settle), so it is a permanent under-count or over-count that only the invoice comparison finds; `max_chars` bounds the size of one call. **One request per check (security major M1 of v10):** `defaults.GUARDRAIL_MAX_REQUESTS = 1` is the single source; `_client` (`guard/bedrock_guardrail.py:28`, which fixes `total_max_attempts` at 2 on line 36) gets a keyword `total_max_attempts: int = 2`; the **runtime** client passes `GUARDRAIL_MAX_REQUESTS`, the start-up client that reads the guardrail's settings keeps 2. **There is no gate retry for the guardrail:** one failed request is a stop, because `injection_check` turns an error into a flagged verdict (5.5); v11's change list said the gate's retry owns repeats, which was wrong (security minor F12). The reserve is `usd_per_unit * units * GUARDRAIL_MAX_REQUESTS`, so if someone raises the constant the reserve rises with it. **Cost of one request (security minor F11):** a transient 5xx or timeout now flags a run (`guard_unavailable`) where the SDK's second attempt might have saved it; E0-S2-7 counts the added flags with a scripted guardrail that fails on 1 percent and on 5 percent of calls (made-up rates) and reports them beside the false-abstain split; if the added false abstains are too many the lead's alternative is `GUARDRAIL_MAX_REQUESTS = 2` (the reserve doubles with it). Test: build the runtime client with a stub that captures the `Config` passed to `boto3.client` and assert `total_max_attempts == GUARDRAIL_MAX_REQUESTS`; mutant: set 2; a text of one unit and of three units reserves one and three prices; a text above `max_chars` makes no request. The detector lets `SpendRefused` rise; `injection_check` handles it per 5.5. No vendor price or unit is in our code. This pulls v9's L-5 into S-2a. The window-only part is in S-1 and works with `llm.kind: fake` (5.2).")
d.rep("`hadavin-sdk gate` gets a required `--max-usd` argument when `llm.kind` is not `fake`", "`hadavin-sdk gate` gets a `--max-usd` argument (added to the `gate` sub-parser, `src/hadavin_sdk/cli.py:90-92`, as `g.add_argument(\"--max-usd\", type=_money, default=None)`, and checked in the `gate` branch at `src/hadavin_sdk/cli.py:146`), required when `llm.kind` is not `fake`")
d.after_line("| 6 | window end |", "| 7 | the guardrail price is the real charge | the vendor bills the guardrail by the unit the operator wrote (5.7) and counts text units as `ceil(len / unit_chars)` | the vendor bills per policy type, per token or per request, or counts units another way | the booked amount is wrong on every guardrail call and **is never corrected** (no settle, no cost field) | every guardrail call, by the ratio of the real unit to the written one | `max_chars` bounds one call; UNVERIFIED; invoice comparison only |\n| 8 | a failed attempt that was not billed costs nothing | the kept-after-failure rule (5.3) | a vendor does not bill a 429 or a 5xx: our total is too high and the agent can stop early | up to `max_call` per failed call; four failed calls stop the day | open availability risk; audit row, status line and card text; owner question O1 |")
